# Portfolio: OmniLib House Centralized Document Architecture

This repository contains a comprehensive documentation suite for **OmniLib House**, a centralized, multi-city library management and peer-to-peer book exchange system.

This project showcases diverse technical documentation relevant to specific audiences. 

**Project Note:** OmniLib House is a fictional system used purely as a conceptual sample. I designed and wrote these document sets to showcase my technical writing skills, information architecture design, and content strategy workflows in a real-world scenario.

## 💡 System Concept Framework Overview
OmniLib House resolves the logistical hurdles of managing multi-city library networks. Key architecture features include:
* **Centralized Logistics Routing (ILLR):** Allows patrons to borrow a physical book in one city and return it to a branch in an entirely different city.
* **Decentralized Custody Exchanges (DCTP):** A peer-to-peer validation framework enabling two users to securely swap books face-to-face while automatically updating account custody records via mobile devices.
* **Integrated Media Networks:** Manages and streams digital assets (ePubs/PDFs) and high-quality video recordings of on-site author events across branches.


## 📂 Repository Directory Guide

Navigate through these modular documentation guides to evaluate specific writing styles based on target audiences:

1. **[System Architecture Specs](/docs/01-architecture-spec.md):** Deep technical overviews and SQL data schemas designed for Systems Architects and Backend Engineers.
2. **[Core API Reference Manual](/docs/02-api-reference.md):** Strongly-typed payload templates, headers, status frameworks, and code blocks (cURL/Python) written for Integration Developers.
3. **[Installation & Operations Playbook](/docs/03-installation-ops-guide.md):** Plain-language technical walkthroughs, environment build steps, and server launch workflows targeted at DevOps Teams and Branch Administrators.
4. **[Internal Librarian Runbook](/docs/04-librarian-runbook.md):** Task-focused workflows and decision-tree guides tailored for library administrators and branch managers.
5. **[Patron User Manual](/docs/05-end-user-guide.md):** Highly accessible instructions written in clear language to guide end-users through advanced system actions (like peer-to-peer book swaps).
6. **[Troubleshooting Matrix](/docs/06-troubleshooting-matrix.md):** Error Matrices, diagnostic commands, and recovery runbooks written for System Administrators and Customer Support Desks.

